TEXT 160 -80 Left 3 ;#380 Twin-tee op-amp oscillator
TEXT 160 -16 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KFVVozlXoOk
TEXT 160 32 Left 2 ;The twin-tee notch in the feedback path leaves the op amp its highest gain at one frequency, and the loop oscillates there.
TEXT 160 920 Left 2 !.include ..\..\LTspice\Models\Microchip\MCP6001_family_RevE_Bordodynov.lib
TEXT 160 960 Left 2 !.ic V(out)=2.6
TEXT 160 1000 Left 2 !.tran 0 300m 0 2u uic
TEXT 160 1040 Left 2 !.step param RTRIM list 300 330 380
TEXT 160 1080 Left 2 !.meas tran VPP_EARLY PP V(OUT) FROM 20m TO 40m
TEXT 160 1120 Left 2 !.meas tran VPP_LATE PP V(OUT) FROM 280m TO 300m
TEXT 160 1160 Left 2 !.meas tran PERIOD TRIG V(OUT)=2.5 RISE=20 TARG V(OUT)=2.5 RISE=30
TEXT 160 1200 Left 2 !.meas tran FREQ PARAM 10/PERIOD
TEXT 160 1264 Left 2 ;The MCP6001 model is the Microchip MCP6001/2/4 family core, and its header states that detailed distortion
TEXT 160 1296 Left 2 ;behaviour is not supported. RTRIM is swept because the loop has no amplitude limit short of the supply rails.
